<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      netstandard2.0 is here for exactly one reason: Fallout.Build.Shared multi-targets it, and its
      own code (FalloutPaths, Notifications) reads these constants. Build.Shared in turn keeps
      netstandard2.0 only so Fallout.SourceGenerators can reference it — a Roslyn generator has to
      be netstandard2.0. Nothing else forces it: no generator and no MSBuild task reads Constants.

      netstandard2.1 is deliberately absent. Core uses no 2.1-only API, so that asset would be
      identical to this one, and a 2.1 consumer resolves netstandard2.0 anyway. Keep new Core code
      netstandard2.0-clean; if it ever needs a 2.1 API, add the target back behind an #if.

      Exit condition: once #442 frees the SourceGenerators cone, Fallout.Build.Shared can drop
      netstandard2.0 and this target goes with it — see #441.
    -->
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Description>The reactor core of Fallout — pure domain types and graph algorithms of the build execution pipeline. No I/O, no process, no console, no logging. References nothing else in the repo.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
